  `activeDownloads` counter; `startNext()` fills up to N slots concurrently. N = new
  `parallelDownloads` setting (default 3), editable under **Settings → Downloads → Song caching**
  ("Parallel downloads", integer input next to "Cache next song"). Pause/cancel/clear correctly
  release slots (cancel only decrements when the item had a live resumable). i18n en/de.
- Shared-song semantics confirmed (no code change): songs in 2+ downloaded collections accumulate
  sources on the index entry; `removeSource` deletes the file only when sources drop to `[]`, so
  deleting one playlist keeps the shared song for the other. Known edge case (deferred): deleting a
  collection while a shared song is still queued cancels that queue item and it won't re-download
  for the surviving collection.

