  lifted row disappearing:
  - **Drag rewrite** (`QueueDrag.js`): window-coordinate measurement is unreliable inside a `Modal`, so the
    provider now computes everything relative to the shared container — both lists are direct children of one
    parent, their `onLayout` `boxY`/`boxH` + the gesture `dy` resolve the drop target, no `measureInWindow`.
    Region detection only engages "Up next" when that box actually exists (a previously absent box captured
    drops); cross-section gap = trailing rows (`index >= targetIndex`) shift `+rowHeight` (the old code
    compared indices across lists); same-list gaps shift per from/target relationship; desktop's bottom-aligned
    queue gets a `bottomPad` correction.
