## 2026-08-30 — FIX: background auto-advance reverts index (same song restarts)
- Report: screen off + natural song end -> same song restarts; next must be pressed 2-3x to
  finally advance. No loop enabled.
- Evidence: instrumented the service + playerCore with logger (Playback events, setIndex,
  nextSong, loadSong). logcat revealed: after a natural end, nextSong setIndex 20 + loadSong 20
  succeeded, then `global.song.index` REVERTED to 19; next presses recomputed setIndex 20 and
  RELOADED track 20 (same song restarts) until a 3rd press finally moved.
- Root cause: songReducer's newSong sets `global.song = { ...state, ...action }` USING REACT'S
  STATE SNAPSHOT. Background advances run through the headless service's fakeSongDispatch and
  mutate global.song but never React's snapshot. The next ordinary React dispatch (useEvent's
  PlaybackState -> setState) then merged the STALE snapshot, reverting global.song's already-
  advanced index/songInfo. Any skip during that window reloaded the current track.
- Fix (2 lines + comment):
  1) songReducer: `state = global.song ?? state` at the top — every transition computes from the
     canonical global.song, never the stale snapshot. React's snapshot lags global.song only, so
     global.song is always the correct base. This kills the revert for good.
  2) servicePlayback: new getSongDispatch() = global.songDispatch || fakeSongDispatch — when the
     app is alive, background advances dispatch to the REAL React reducer, so UI (and global.song)
     move together; fake dispatch stays as cold-headless fallback.
- Instrumentation kept (Settings -> Logs / logcat) pending user's on-device verdict.
- Installed: connected phone only (tablet R52Y80837NY offline).

## 2026-09-29 — Player: queue swipe-up overlay, cover-tap lyrics, cast to Home (`beccb47`)
- Shipped TODO #36. Bottom button row deleted; its height moved into playerContainer's
  paddingBottom (30 -> 82) so the control cluster stayed exactly where #35 measured it.
  Queue became a whole-window overlay (QueueSheet.js) instead of a third `preview` value.
- Cast moved to Home as a sibling of the refresh control. Home only, not every tab.
- Radio badge removed from the transport row (display only; "End radio" stays in the ... menu).
- Verified on R5CY71GYKWF: no crash, controls unmoved, gesture works from the black band.

### The three platform traps (this is the reusable part)
1. PanResponder fills x0/y0 only at GRANT time (PanResponder.js:471); they stay 0 through the
   whole should-set phase. A move-phase handler testing g.y0 is testing `0 > something` — always
   false. Use g.moveY. Symptom: gesture completely dead, capture handler visibly firing.
2. onMoveShouldSetResponder on an ancestor LOSES: the pressable under the finger wins the
   responder at touch-START, so the parent is never asked again. Use the *Capture* variant.
3. A prop-less View is COLLAPSED out of the native hierarchy on Android, so a touch on plain
   empty space never enters the responder system and delivers no MOVE events at all. Proven by
   logging touch coordinates: y~600 and y~898 gave a DOWN and nothing more; buttons and the
   title worked. This is why the swipe looked like it needed "button precision". Fix: a
   neverTake onStartShouldSetResponder on the containers, and a real drag strip that claims on
   DOWN where nothing interactive is underneath.
4. Android's bottom-edge BACK gesture is consumed by the platform before any PanResponder sees
   it; it surfaced as Modal.onRequestClose closing the whole player. Confirmed with a stack
   trace. onRequestClose now dismisses by layer order: queue -> lyrics -> player.

### Process lessons (I slipped on these)
- Instrument with console.log: it survives the release build (no transform-remove-console in
  babel.config.js) and logcat captures it under ReactNativeJS. Guessing cost far more cycles
  than one instrumented build.
- adb `input swipe` does NOT generate MOVE events the app sees (only DOWN/UP), so gestures
  cannot be verified from the CLI — the user has to swipe. Taps do work.
- Do NOT do line-number-based deletion across edits. It silently removed a JSX opening tag
  (`<TimeBar />` and the transport row's `<View>`) and crashed the player on open. Use
  context-anchored string replacement, and assert on the JSX structure afterwards.
- Python read/write normalises CRLF -> LF. SlideControl.js and Home.js are CRLF in git; they
  showed as whole-file rewrites until the line endings were restored.
- Commit between build/install iterations. I did ~10 uncommitted build cycles this session.

